# Findings

## High — The causal reset/marker branch still lacks a deterministic production-seam regression

The new behavior is in `discoverMusicSession` and `ManagedRuntimeProbe.starting()` (`packages/music-core/session/client.ts:766-780`, `packages/music-core/session/config.ts:888-894`), but no focused test drives a real reset endpoint together with a live marker through that branch. `owned daemon readiness closes the transient hello-reset window` uses an injected discovery function that returns only `missing` and `healthy`; despite its name, it creates no socket reset and exercises neither the new discovery classification nor the config authority. The existing live-marker test has no socket, while the existing reset-peer test has no marker.

The concurrent suite passing is useful integration evidence, but it is not deterministic proof of the minimized causal condition and can pass without observing the reset window. Add direct coverage showing a retryable reset plus an independently valid live marker becomes `starting` without cleanup authority, while malformed/unmarked/dead-or-changed-marker peers remain terminal and untouched. This is also required direct coverage for the newly touched `config.ts` authority rule.

## High — Required real-host and red-before-green evidence is still missing for the current implementation

Round 3 changed production behavior again but records no fresh exact OpenCode `opencode2 v0.0.0-next-17386` or Pi `0.84.0` checkout-loaded initialization. Package smokes and the core daemon smoke do not substitute for those required regular-pane host checks. The only retained red commands in earlier results still contain `...`, and there is still no retained failing run of the causal regression before its production fix.

Before approval, provide an exact agent-runnable red/green loop and the required current-code isolated host observations, including versions, absolute checkout entries, process/runtime artifacts, host-visible result, and owned cleanup. Complete the omitted parent/non-Apnea diff and generated-debris gates as well.

## Medium — Long split daemon diagnostics are discarded rather than bounded and truncated

`packages/music-core/session/client.ts:926-929` discards the entire pending line once it exceeds 512 bytes before a newline arrives. Thus a daemon-prefixed causal error longer than 512 bytes, delivered across normal stream chunks, produces no diagnostic at all rather than the required bounded/truncated diagnostic. The test sends a long non-daemon line and only a short daemon line, so it does not cover this case.

Retain a byte-bounded prefix of an eligible daemon line while discarding the remainder, test a multichunk daemon-prefixed line over the limit, and assert the typed exit code/signal/diagnostic propagates through `connectOrStartMusicSessionEffect` to the host acquisition boundary—not only through the launch object's accessor.
